Description: Out-of-band USB serial console multiplexer
 oob-usb-serial turns a small Linux host (such as a Raspberry Pi Zero with a
 USB hub and several USB-to-serial adapters) into an out-of-band access box for
 network and server equipment.
 .
 It discovers every attached USB-to-serial adapter, matches each one against an
 optional per-device configuration keyed by its stable udev serial identifier,
 and opens all of them as named windows inside a single detached tmux session,
 each running tio on the adapter's stable /dev/serial/by-id path. Baud rate,
 data bits, parity, stop bits and flow control are configurable per device,
 with sensible global defaults for adapters that are not explicitly mapped.
 .
 A systemd service can bring the session up at boot, and an opt-in login
 snippet attaches a dedicated user straight into the consoles on SSH login.
